        "ephanna": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Session 12 council chamber fight includes the Players, the Wolf, Thalia, and multiple Guards (including reinforcements); no explicit evidence confirms council members are present during the fight.\n\nBased on OBSERVED facts:\n- Players are actively in the council chamber scene (they recount their story to the council and are \u201cactively in battle\u201d).\n- the Wolf is explicitly in the Council Room and even \u201cstanding at Thalia\u2019s shoulder.\u201d\n- Thalia (Commander of the Guard) is present alongside the Wolf and becomes combat-active.\n- Guards are present and escalating: some are already positioned (\u201cplaced in a ring along the wall\u201d) and more are \u201cbeing drawn here as reinforcements,\u201d with combat actions occurring.\n\nNo entity entry confirms council members remain physically present once the fight breaks out, so their presence is uncertain.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Combatants: Players (group of 6), the Wolf (illusory decoys), Thalia, multiple Guards (including elite/corrupted variants)\n- Positioning: Wolf at Thalia\u2019s shoulder; guards along walls and reinforcing\n- Environment: Large circular chamber with magical defenses (illusory walls, runes)\n- Escalation: Guards actively entering; fight already underway with environmental hazards and confusion effects",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_campaign_general_notes_1",
      "question": "Who are the Shepherds, and what god or power do they answer to?",
