      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the wizards; he treats the cult as a serious arcane threat and pushes for aggressive magical detection and containment, including a lockdown.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright is the wizard representative on the council (OBSERVED: \u201cRepresentative of the Arcane,\u201d Head of the Wizard\u2019s College). His stance on the cult is driven by alarm and urgency: he views the corrupted meat as a perversion of magic (CANON) and is deeply troubled by the dark magic involved (CANON).\n\nHis \u201cangle\u201d is proactive and arcane-heavy. He plans to:\n- Magically lock the city down (OBSERVED)\n- Use rune-based detection to locate corruption (OBSERVED)\n- Deploy Wizard\u2019s College resources to detect and counteract the cult (OBSERVED)\n\nHe takes the threat seriously and is among the first to present a concrete plan, favoring magical surveillance and containment over slower or purely mundane approaches.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Headmaster of the Wizard\u2019s College; council\u2019s arcane representative  \n- Alignment toward cult: Sees it as dangerous, corrupting magic that must be countered  \n- Strategy: Magical lockdown, detection spells, coordinated arcane response  \n- Personality: Brilliant, inventive, but easily distracted; currently deeply concerned by the threat",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
