      "answer": "TL;DR: Torrin represents the Guilds as Master Smith, Rurik oversees infrastructure as Chief Architect, and Merril\u2019s council role is not defined in the provided context.\n\nMerril:\n- The projection contains no information about Merril\u2019s role or job on the council. Cannot determine from current data.\n\nTorrin Flamescale:\n- Job on council: Representative of the Guilds; Master Smith  \n- Source: OBSERVED role and title confirm he speaks for the craft guilds in council matters.\n\nRurik Stonehammer:\n- Job on council: Representative of Infrastructure; Chief Architect  \n- Source: CANON role plus OBSERVED title align\u2014he is responsible for the city\u2019s structural integrity and infrastructure concerns.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Governance: Council includes faction representatives (Guilds, Infrastructure).\n- City Concerns: Defense integrity, hidden passages, and infrastructure are active issues (Rurik\u2019s domain).\n- Guild Influence: Craft and trade interests are represented through Torrin.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
