      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead\u2014specifically **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014with Bonogo taking the head.\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states for **the Wolf**: he both \u201cescapes\u201d and \u201cAttempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible,\u201d but also has the terminal condition **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** Because decapitation is a terminal outcome and Bonogo\u2019s role explicitly includes \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it,\u201d the **current, authoritative state is that the Wolf is dead**. The escape/invisibility reflects an earlier phase of the encounter, superseded by the later kill.\n\nSo at fight\u2019s end:\n- The Wolf is no longer an active threat.\n- His body is separated, with Bonogo in possession of the head.\n- Any prior invisibility or escape attempt is resolved by his death.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- physical_condition (OBSERVED): \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d; previously Invisible\n- operational_status (OBSERVED): attempted escape earlier, but overridden by death\n- role: central adversary in the council chamber battle\n- Bonogo role (OBSERVED): \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it\u201d",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
