      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence in the projection that Thalia is corrupted like the guards; her behavior is tied to The Wolf\u2019s influence (orders/betrayal context), which suggests something different, but it\u2019s not explicitly defined.\n\nFrom the available facts:\n- **Guards** (OBSERVED) show clear corruption markers: \u201cAll checked guards have an oily sheen to their eyes,\u201d along with mutation/merging effects.\n- **The Wolf** (OBSERVED) also has \u201can oily sheen to his eyes,\u201d reinforcing that as a corruption indicator.\n- **Thalia** is only referenced indirectly: The Wolf \u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d and there\u2019s a \u201cBetrayal (as presented to Thalia)\u201d context.\n\nThere is **no explicit mention** of Thalia having oily eyes, physical corruption, or exposure to corrupted meat.\n\nSo, based strictly on the projection:\n- Thalia is **not confirmed corrupted like the guards**.\n- Her actions are more likely tied to **manipulation, coercion, or deception by The Wolf**, but the exact mechanism is **not specified**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Guards (OBSERVED): oily sheen eyes; corruption tied to meat; physical transformation effects\n- The Wolf (OBSERVED): oily sheen eyes; issues commands; manipulative role\n- Thalia: no recorded physical corruption markers; acts under The Wolf\u2019s direction",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
