      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no direct evidence that Thalia is untrustworthy, but the situation around her is volatile\u2014nothing confirms she\u2019s compromised, yet caution is warranted.\n\nBased on OBSERVED facts, Thalia is involved in planning and coordination: Caelynn gives her a concrete task (\u201cbring a potion to Lesandra at the Wizard\u2019s College\u201d) and is \u201ctalking with Thalia about the plans,\u201d which suggests a baseline level of trust from at least one party member.\n\nHowever, there is a notable red flag in events: \u201cStafl attacks Thalia after being revived.\u201d This does not prove Thalia is compromised\u2014Stafl\u2019s mental state includes being \u201ccharmed\u201d and \u201cwill never fully trust anyone other than self,\u201d which could explain erratic aggression\u2014but it does indicate tension or suspicion directed at her in play.\n\nNo facts mention Thalia showing corruption (e.g., oily eyes) or acting against the party.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Trust signals: Entrusted with mission-critical delivery (Caelynn \u2192 Thalia) [OBSERVED]\n- Social position: Included in planning discussions [OBSERVED]\n- Threat indicators: Target of sudden intra-party attack (Stafl) [OBSERVED]\n- Corruption signs: None recorded [OBSERVED]\n\nConclusion: She\u2019s provisionally trustworthy, but the scene supports keeping an eye on her rather than fully relying on her without verification.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_4_v2",
      "question": "If the council keeps talking and doesn't act, what bites us?",
      "strict_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
