      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room shows signs of chaotic deception and corruption\u2014most notably the Wolf\u2019s body, **decapitated; head removed from body**, lingering illusion effects, and guards with the same oily-eyed corruption.\n\nAfter the fight, the strongest visual anchor is the Wolf himself: his corpse lies where he fell, **decapitated; head removed from body** (OBSERVED). This is a clear, undeniable proof of both his defeat and his importance.\n\nBeyond that, the room still carries the aftermath of his tactics:\n- Illusory confusion likely just faded\u2014evidence of where duplicates stood or misled the party (CANON: illusion use).\n- The council chamber was an active combat space, so expect signs of disruption\u2014movement, positioning, and possibly scattered guards.\n\nWhat stands out most is the guards:\n- Multiple guards show **an oily sheen to their eyes** (OBSERVED), directly mirroring the Wolf\u2019s corruption.\n- Survivors are tense and unsettled (OBSERVED mental state), and their positioning suggests they were either part of the conflict or struggling to contain it.\n\nThere\u2019s also an important environmental implication:\n- The Wolf had been attempting to escape via a **secret passage beneath the council chamber** (OBSERVED goal), so signs of that exit\u2014disturbed flooring, a hidden mechanism, or recent movement\u2014may now be noticeable.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defeat evidence: **decapitated; head removed from body**\n- Corruption signs: guards with oily sheen in eyes\n- Illusion aftermath: confusion/disruption from duplicates\n- Hidden infrastructure: possible access to secret passage beneath chamber\n- Guard state: tense, reactive, partially compromised",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
