      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead at end of Session 12\u2014he was **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014and had shown clear signs of corruption prior (oily sheen in eyes).\n\nThe OBSERVED physical_condition includes the terminal outcome **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, which overrides earlier escape/invisibility states. While he previously **\u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d** and was **\u201cAttempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible\u201d**, those are superseded by the confirmed kill. Additionally, Bonogo\u2019s role explicitly notes he **removed the Wolf\u2019s head**, reinforcing the finality.\n\nCorruption status: prior to death, the Wolf **\u201chas an oily sheen to his eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED), indicating active corruption. There is no evidence of that corruption being cured before death.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (OBSERVED, terminal)\n- Corruption Indicator: **\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED)\n- Operational Status (pre-death): escaping while invisible\n- Faction/Alignment: cultist; betrayer of Mirathorn\n- Role: central adversary in council chamber confrontation\n\nCurrent state: dead, formerly corrupted, no longer active.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
