      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive saboteur manipulating events; after, he is **decapitated; head removed from body** and characterized by desperation, regret, and signs of corruption.\n\nBefore the fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **cultist** and **second-in-command of the guard**, actively undermining the council.\n- He uses **illusory duplicates** and deception to confuse both players and council members.\n- His behavior is controlled and strategic: steering discussions, issuing orders (e.g., to Thalia), and attempting escape via invisibility and secret tunnels.\n- Alignment-wise, he has **betrayed the city of Mirathorn** and acts as a saboteur.\n\nAfter the fight (OBSERVED):\n- His state becomes terminal: **Decapitated; head removed from body**.\n- His mental state shifts sharply\u2014**begging to be killed, desperate, feels regret**\u2014indicating either breaking control or awareness of corruption.\n- Physical corruption is evident: **Wolf has an oily sheen to his eyes**.\n- No longer an active manipulator; he becomes a source of information (players plan Speak with Dead).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Saboteur \u2192 Corpse (post-fight)\n- Mental State: Calculated deception \u2192 Desperate, regretful\n- Physical Condition: Illusion-using, mobile \u2192 **Decapitated; head removed from body**\n- Alignment Context: Hidden traitor \u2192 Exposed, corrupted figure",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
