      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was **not corrupted**\u2014she was **ensorcelled and manipulated by the Wolf**, who is the actual corrupting influence tied to the \u201coily sheen\u201d effect.\n\nThalia\u2019s state is consistently OBSERVED as **\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d** and **\u201censcorcelled (unbeknownst to her)\u201d**, with **no oily sheen to her eyes**, which is the established marker of corruption in others (e.g., guards, the Wolf). Her mental state includes **\u201cInnocent\u201d** and **\u201cCharmed status ended\u201d**, and she can be **convinced of the Wolf\u2019s betrayal**, all of which point to manipulation rather than true allegiance or corruption.\n\nBy contrast, the Wolf is explicitly tied to corruption: he has an **\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d**, is a **cultist**, and actively **orders Thalia to attack** and manipulates events. This establishes him as the source of influence, not a partner.\n\nSo the relationship is: **the Wolf corrupts and deceives; Thalia is a compromised instrument, not a willing agent**.\n\nNotably, the Wolf ultimately ends with: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body;\u201d** which likely breaks or explains the end of his control over others like Thalia.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia: ensorcelled (unaware), no oily sheen, loyal to city, manipulated by Wolf, can be persuaded\n- The Wolf: cultist, oily sheen (corrupted), deceptive, issues commands to Thalia, source of ensorcellment",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
